Z||000004||stsmithgt||05-30-2001||05:18 PM||||Everybody seems to be talking about cracked manifolds.  What about warped manifolds?  Have you ever put a staight edge to an exhaust manifold.  Those things like to twist and curl.  It can be pretty bad.  Gaskets can blow out and sound like a tick or, a good example I just read, like an old volkswagon.  I'm picking up some manifolds today that I had checked out for cracks and machined to fit better (I hope).  Good luck with your ticks out there. I'm finished <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flagcheck.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
